  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.300): (1) It is unlawful for any person to enter the following places when he or she knowingly possesses or knowingly has under his or her control a weapon:\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.300): (f) State capitol buildings and west capitol campus grounds; or\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.300): (g) City, town, county, or other municipality buildings used in connection with meetings of the governing body, as defined in RCW 42.30.020, of the city, town, county, or other municipality.\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.300): (11) Subsection (1)(f) of this section does not apply to the concealed carry of a pistol by any member of the legislature who has a valid concealed pistol license issued under RCW 9.41.070.\nSec. 1 (RCW 9.41.300): (13) Any person violating subsection (1) of this section is guilty of a gross misdemeanor."
}